{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['repeat_experiment_id']='81237e6441414088bfb2079263cc63ec-experiment'\nd['rationale']=d['rationale']+\\\" Reproducibility question: the three-voter simultaneous-restart experiment is repeated once from its retained inputs in a clean copy, because the progress claim (no leader while every voter holds the configuration only in its log) is the headline liveness consequence and currently rests on a single scored execution with its control.\\\"\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['rationale']=par['rationale']+\\\" Summary of the current account for this question: the trigger is RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a CommitTrackingLogStore, a log whose newest configuration entry is at or below the persisted commit index, and no snapshot whose ConfigurationIndex covers that entry. Under that trigger the restarted node reconstructs its configuration only from the snapshot, so three consequence classes follow, each with retained control-backed receipts: (a) a missing membership context - empty configuration when there is no snapshot, which stops all campaigns and leaves a live quorum unable to elect (receipts 430d7ba602ed4666bdfe63a96c71e2fc, 4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a, 7afe8c0403874dbeb0a917a3ee9ed837); (b) decisions taken from a stale base - a single AddVoter becomes the two-server change {A,B,C}->{A,B,E}, which silently drops a voter, and with a partitioned old voter produces concurrent leaders over the same log, truncation of the entry the stale leader had committed and divergent FSM state (receipts d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740, 6f9feceeefb245c288a7fd1f4497b83c, 11dea1fdcb6d4f089a0d... and e5ad9e5149fa4255b61e7826bf6b8064); (c) stale membership accounting - a resurrected removed voter or a forgotten added voter makes the leader accept writes that the configuration committed in the log has not acknowledged (receipts 226f9762f0b444f69c154b35fe0788f3 with 7adf927d528b4a74942c03b155aa8557, and b1daa1f4c9444b8d857bc7e0ab761691 with ec2c61af79bd42d7a5fe00657b7aeb22). Boundary: a snapshot covering the newest configuration entry, or leaving the flag at its default, removes every one of these observations in the controls, and no in-protocol repair exists once the stale configuration is adopted (nothing re-reads the log for configurations; only an installed snapshot or an operator restart without the flag repairs it).\\\"\npar['limitations'].append(\\\"The consolidated summary names receipt 11dea1fdcb6d4f089a373fe6c1d3a36e in shortened form together with the other dual-majority receipts; the full ids and parsed indices remain in the executions map and in the individual consequence paragraphs above.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
